{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3","id":1305783,"title":"Do you play Ex3?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-18T12:29:34-07:00","id":1305783,"title":"Do you play Ex3?","content":"I'm curious, how many people are actually playing this latest edition?<br /> <br /> I'm currently just reading the books, and sometimes I come here to the forums to see if there's been any exciting news.<br /> <br /> How about you, or the players near you? Would you say Ex3 is popular as a gaming option? Or is it more like a setting that people like to read but can't actually get the time, the friends, or whatever to play it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T12:36:30-07:00","id":1305786,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been running the same campaign since the core book went to print. So, yes. As far as local gamer scene goes in the Portland Oregon metro area, I don\u2019t know. I don\u2019t often go to gaming stores to play or buy books. Since all of my players are busy professionals we play as often as we are able, sometimes it\u2019s 3 times a month sometimes it\u2019s once every 6 weeks depending on who\u2019s traveling at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T12:37:47-07:00","id":1305787,"title":"","content":"I've been running a single 3e Solar campaign called Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns for 3-4 years. Of course, since 3e was only an anticipated dream when we started we played under a Fate Core reskin until the core book released. There's 5 players, two twilights, no zenith, and one each of the other castes.<br /> <br /> Most of the players have hit E4 by now, we're planning to wrap the whole game before the end of the year / an additional player moves.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I think I'm in the only gaming group in town that plays something other than D&amp;D or Pathfinder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T12:37:58-07:00","id":1305788,"title":"","content":"I'm playing it and enjoying it a lot. I am currently in two live voice games that play weekly. I am also in a few PBP games. While on non-Exalted-focused sites I haven't seen as much Exalted interest as D&amp;D-et-al, when I do see it, it's nearly always 3e as opposed to 2e or 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T12:47:31-07:00","id":1305789,"title":"","content":"I'm playing roughly once a month with my local friends. Half of my group is running another game with their coworkers (all of whom it's their first table-top RPG ever and love it). It's complex but proving to be worth the effort for everyone involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T12:52:59-07:00","id":1305790,"title":"","content":"A little bit more about my experience..<br /> <br /> I'm pretty introverted, so my experience with gaming outside my immediate friends group is pretty sparse. For all I know there ~could~ be half a dozen Exalted games going on in my area... but I'm thinking that's unlikely, and Exalted books don't get stocked to lure new gamers in anymore (alas, market forces problems).<br /> <br /> I did play in an Exalted 3rd edition game at Gencon in 2017, had a ton of fun in a Spaghetti Western meets Studio Ghiblli mash-up one shot. <br /> <br /> Played a 2.X Exalted game the next year (sadly, no 3rd edition games at the con) but had an absolute blast anyway.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I think finding a group is 80% luck and 20% putting yourself out there. A group of folks for a niche game in a niche hobby is a hard thing to come by.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sure do miss the days of healthy, populous chat games though; those were good times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:26:09-07:00","id":1305798,"title":"","content":"I have been playing 3e regularly for the last two years, so yes, I\u00b4m.<br /> <br /> Although I stopped my current campaign a month and a half ago, and have been playing an Unknown Armies one, mostly so I can rest with a lighter system for a while: the last Exalted game had some pretty intense and long battles, and they are pretty mentally exhausting :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T14:26:03-07:00","id":1305808,"title":"","content":"I played Ex3 for some months intermittently with a handful of my usual gaming buds, the Exalted veteran was our Storyteller, but that game is in hiatus now. Lotsa shenanigans, it was fun! Our Twilight's player tried running a game of his own with different characters but we didn't get more than two sessions and a few interactions in, unfortunately. I've been meaning to run Dragon-Blooded myself, but I have to prepare well and I've been running/thinking of other stuff in the meantime.<br /> <br /> I think on its own the setting definitely has a lot to <i>talk about</i>, but in some ways it almost distracts from running a game, if that makes sense. It comes up pretty often in discussion with my online tabletop circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T14:50:27-07:00","id":1305812,"title":"","content":"Exalted is definitely more of an rpg book club than being actively played. If you look on Google trends vs 2004 there's about 8 to 12% of the activity now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T15:34:31-07:00","id":1305830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1305812#post1305812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you look on Google trends vs 2004 there's about 8 to 12% of the activity now.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?<br /> <br /> <br /> With my old friends from Uni, I run a (quite new) Lunars game and play 2 Mixed games, one of which I used to run. We alternate them on Sundays, so basically I'm playing or running Exalted 3 out of 4 Sundays. I'd say I've run/played it every 1-2 weeks since a bit before 3rd edition came out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, in the city where I live, the rpg club does a lot of DnD but does do plenty of other games too (some classics like Paranoia and Call of Cthulu, some newer games like Monsterhearts, Numinera, Lady Blackbird, etc). But no-one seems to have heard of Exalted. In fact, when I told my DnD group I played a fantasy game made by the same people who make Vampire (which some of them have played, and all of them have heard of), they were surprised they'd never heard of Exalted.<br /> <br /> My old gaming group in uni was massively into White Wolf, I think way more than half the games were White Wolf, but I don't know if that's an era thing (were White Wolf games much more popular in the past than now? My Exalted group's average is probably 34ish, my DnD group's average age is more like 28) or just those happened to be popular in that city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-18-2019, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T16:06:29-07:00","id":1305836,"title":"","content":"I play it all the time in different mediums and with different groups. The only thing I don't get to do is to actually &quot;play&quot; myself, since I'm stricken by the ST curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T16:28:39-07:00","id":1305842,"title":"","content":"I run a mixed game and a Dragon-Blooded game, I play in three games with a fourth starting soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T16:58:59-07:00","id":1305847,"title":"","content":"Not currently, but got a decent amount of in already. So between campaigns and looking for a new group (I don't have a consistent group so that's always an issue regardless of what I'm trying to play).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:01:10-07:00","id":1305849,"title":"","content":"I do not play EX3.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because I am afflicted with the curse of the forever ST and my only chances to actually PLAY my favorite RPG of all time are but fleeting moments that do nothing but leave me starved for more.<br /> <br /> That said, I have been running it for, shit, approaching or possibly just exceeding four years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:39:12-07:00","id":1305861,"title":"","content":"Currently in a round-robin game with four other players, it's my turn as ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T18:12:21-07:00","id":1305865,"title":"","content":"I'd be down to play Ex3, but I've never found a gaming group that wanted to play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T18:16:10-07:00","id":1305866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1305865#post1305865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be down to play Ex3, but I've never found a gaming group that wanted to play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you tried online play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T18:34:31-07:00","id":1305874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1305830#post1305830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean?<br /> <br /> <br /> With my old friends from Uni, I run a (quite new) Lunars game and play 2 Mixed games, one of which I used to run. We alternate them on Sundays, so basically I'm playing or running Exalted 3 out of 4 Sundays. I'd say I've run/played it every 1-2 weeks since a bit before 3rd edition came out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Look at this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20rpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20rpg\" target=\"_blank\"> Error 429 (Too Many Requests)!!1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20rpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20rpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20game\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20game\" target=\"_blank\"> Error 429 (Too Many Requests)!!1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20game\" target=\"_blank\"> https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=exalted%20game </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T00:20:28-07:00","id":1305920,"title":"","content":"That's very interesting.<br /> And very different to DnD.<br /> <br /> When was 2nd ed out? Because it looks like Exalted's publicity decline was way before 3rd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T01:25:45-07:00","id":1305930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1305920#post1305920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very interesting.<br /> And very different to DnD.<br /> <br /> When was 2nd ed out? Because it looks like Exalted's publicity decline was way before 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>February 2006, per the WW fandom wiki.<br /> <br /> Comparing against the release list... ah. The &quot;exalted rpg&quot; search peaks roundabout Savant and Sorcerer's release. Not sure about the next major peak; that might be the comic's #0 issue in 2005. The last 25+ peak is... interestingly, a couple of months prior to Return of the Scarlet Empress. After traditional print supplements stop, it never reaches that high again.<br /> <br /> For &quot;exalted game&quot;, the last peak that gets close to 50 is about the time of MoEP: Dragon-Blooded's release.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I can derive any conclusions from those, apart from saying the peak of people searching was during 1e, and that there was a bit of a dropoff in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 04-19-2019, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T01:44:16-07:00","id":1305931,"title":"","content":"I wonder if other less well-known RPGs had a similar drop-off when print books faded away.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I first saw Exalted at my friendly local gaming store, and picked up Dragonblood 2nd ed and then later the Core because my friends had mentioned it and the art looked like a cool kung-fu book.<br /> <br /> But now if I go into my local gaming store, there's a whole bunch of completely different games from what I used to see back in the day, and Exalted isn't one of them (seems like DnD, some Monte Cook stuff, Call of Cthulu, Savage Worlds which I've never played, Apocalypse World, etc). It was never big enough to sustain itself off word of mouth like DnD. Nor does it get advertised by connected games/media like Vampire, L5R, Star Wars, WFRP, Shadowrun, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-19-2019, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T02:39:33-07:00","id":1305938,"title":"","content":"Nope. Love the fictional setting, interested in how the system plays out and like talking about both (subject to constraints on my understanding how the system plays out!), but play Ex3 I do not. <br /> <br /> (This probably comes through in my preferences in discussions for &quot;Characters as compelling fictional characters and the setting as an compelling fictional place for an intelligent, well read fantasy audience that knows a thing or two about real world history and economics, and mythology &quot; rather than &quot;A setting that facilitates adventure and characters that can fit being played and STd around a game table and have it be fun and not degenerate into a toxic situation&quot;. Probably a useful disclaimer on some of what I post!).<br /> <br /> Re; Exalted popularity, my opinion is pretty much that the popularity was gonna decline with the popularity of the main influences that were about when Ex1 was first published, as geek culture moved back towards more Anglo-American (though not necessarily Tolkien-esque) fantasy and sci-fi, and to Marvel comics. (Like, I'd go on a tangent here and argue about how the '90s jrpg and anime and wuxia influences, and their parent cultural influences, in Exalted are more than just surface influences and substantial to how the setting is politically and substantially construed and constructed and have most appeal within a base of familiarity with that (which is less common in the marketplace since the mid '00s). But that would be a major tangent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:03:07-07:00","id":1305942,"title":"","content":"I think it's a very good point though. Maybe that's a bigger point than the lack of printed books (which is an issue for many games).<br /> <br /> <br /> I was looking at this thread on RPGnet: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/what-are-you-playing-running-in-2019.840578/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...n-2019.840578/</a><br /> <br /> There's a lot of games mentioned (so you can also see the explosion in games available), and it seems there's quite a few games that are quite popular which I'm not really familiar with, as they're fairly new, like Coriolis, Savage Worlds and Masks.<br /> <br /> But looking at the games, they do mostly seem to be DnD-fantasy clones (different rules, but a similar aesthetic) or sci-fi, and a bit of horror and superheroes*. And in horror games, Vampire is still one of the big ones.<br /> And there are other Onyx Path games mentioned, like Pugmire.<br /> <br /> *Which maybe is unsurprising, considering the Marvel films, as you mentioned.<br /> <br /> Exalted is barely mentioned (it comes up a bit on RPG.net's discussions, but not a ton), but neither is Legends of the Wulin, Anima, and other Asian-inspired games. Even L5R isn't nearly as popular as it used to be, when I put &quot;L5R RPG&quot; into google trends, it's searched for less than 25% of the amount it was searched for in 2005, and that's despite recently releasing a new edition and having a popular card game advertising it.<br /> <br /> DnD's never tried doing another Oriental Adventures since 3rd ed, and none of the popular settings are East Asia-inspired. So presumably they don't see a market.<br /> <br /> So I think you're probably right Ghosthead, the interest in Anime/Wuxia-fantasy rpgs is probably much less than it was back when Exalted 1st ed was released.<br /> <br /> My group of players, who have an Exalted game every Sunday, include two people who've lived in China (me for 4 years, another guy for 1 year but also his wife is Chinese), and some big anime fans (they're currently watching every Gundam series in order). We used to often hang out and watch Kung-fu or East Asian historical action films, most of us have read the Chinese classics (Romance of the Three Kingdoms, Outlaws of the Water Margin, etc).<br /> <br /> Whereas, despite some of my DnD group being into anime, none of them have ever said &quot;hey, we should play an anime-inspired game&quot;. Nor are any of them into Wuxia. And I don't think any of the games being run in my city's rpg club are anime-esque. Dunno why.<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously, Exalted has moved slightly away from anime towards classical Graeco-Roman myth (swords and sandals stuff), but that's not a genre that seems really big either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-19-2019, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:42:33-07:00","id":1305954,"title":"","content":"Yup, running a game with my regular crew of many years. We take turns (or dive into board games). We're just on five games into the chronicle but its going well so far. Finding the system demanding but generally rewarding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T12:52:26-07:00","id":1306068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1305931#post1305931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if other less well-known RPGs had a similar drop-off when print books faded away.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I first saw Exalted at my friendly local gaming store, and picked up Dragonblood 2nd ed and then later the Core because my friends had mentioned it and the art looked like a cool kung-fu book.<br /> <br /> But now if I go into my local gaming store, there's a whole bunch of completely different games from what I used to see back in the day, and Exalted isn't one of them (seems like DnD, some Monte Cook stuff, Call of Cthulu, Savage Worlds which I've never played, Apocalypse World, etc). It was never big enough to sustain itself off word of mouth like DnD. Nor does it get advertised by connected games/media like Vampire, L5R, Star Wars, WFRP, Shadowrun, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a comparison of D&amp;D over time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=D%26D,Dungeons%20and%20Dragons\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=D%26D,Dungeons%20and%20Dragons\" target=\"_blank\"> Error 429 (Too Many Requests)!!1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=D%26D,Dungeons%20and%20Dragons\" target=\"_blank\"> https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=D%26D,Dungeons%20and%20Dragons </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Shadowrun<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=shadowrun%20rpg,shadowrun%20game\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=shadowrun%20rpg,shadowrun%20game\" target=\"_blank\"> Error 429 (Too Many Requests)!!1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=shadowrun%20rpg,shadowrun%20game\" target=\"_blank\"> https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=shadowrun%20rpg,shadowrun%20game </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pathfinder<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=pathfinder%20rpg,pathfinder%20game\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=pathfinder%20rpg,pathfinder%20game\" target=\"_blank\"> Error 429 (Too Many Requests)!!1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=pathfinder%20rpg,pathfinder%20game\" target=\"_blank\"> https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=pathfinder%20rpg,pathfinder%20game </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd say over all there's a downward trend of interest in RPG's -- mostly I think that board games in the same time have become way more popular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=table%20top%20rpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=table%20top%20rpg\" target=\"_blank\"> Error 429 (Too Many Requests)!!1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=table%20top%20rpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;geo=US&amp;q=table%20top%20rpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T15:28:52-07:00","id":1306095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1305942#post1305942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, Exalted has moved slightly away from anime towards classical Graeco-Roman myth (swords and sandals stuff), but that's not a genre that seems really big either.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, I guess 3e feels like it's upping the volume Tanith Lee-S&amp;S tone a bit, more than anything else (helped by Minton being pretty good at writing work that hits that feel?). But again, yeah, not mega popular either!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T19:35:34-07:00","id":1306146,"title":"","content":"Currently playing in a PbP game on GitP forums that we've been doing for...about a year and a half now. It's slow-paced as we've all got busy lives, but a ton of fun. I honestly spent all day today thinking about what my character will do next when it is the right time to post.<br /> <br /> Check out section 1 of our game here!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?543906-The-Lotus-Blossoms\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...Lotus-Blossoms</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:16:21-07:00","id":1306156,"title":"","content":"No, I'm not in a 3E game at the moment, though I've tried playing and running 3E several times. Many of the players in those attempts have played some variation of 1E or 2E, but the 3E system never really clicked for any of the groups I play with locally, though one attempt did start a mid-length campaign using Exalted setting using other rules. The online play-by-post community that I play in sometimes has nowhere near as much 3E activity as the old editions had back when they were releasing books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 04-19-2019, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T22:39:32-07:00","id":1306179,"title":"","content":"I run Exalted 3e, does that count? It's been the most exciting, mechanically engaging version of the game that I've ever run, and I've been doing this since 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T22:56:11-07:00","id":1306181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1306179#post1306179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run Exalted 3e, does that count? It's been the most exciting, mechanically engaging version of the game that I've ever run, and I've been doing this since 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. Running/playing since First Edition (and we're talking &quot;Book of Three Circles was newest book&quot; first edition.) and I'm 100% on the 3rd Edition Best Edition band wagon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T23:30:35-07:00","id":1306186,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve run games of Exalted off and on since 1e and I\u2019m currently in three games of 3e right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T01:30:45-07:00","id":1306200,"title":"","content":"I am the ST for a game right now. <br /> <br /> EDIT: Ignore that bit about the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 05-04-2019, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T01:32:01-07:00","id":1306201,"title":"","content":"My Abyssals game started before 3rd ed was out, so we're still in 2.5E. Haven't given any thought to converting over because of the major homebrew investment it would take to make both Abyssals and the Drive and Firearms Charms playable in EX3, but I do have serious system envy. I've run and played a handful of one-shots in 3E and I can't wait to play a full campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T02:47:03-07:00","id":1306205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1306200#post1306200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heavily, heavily streamline the mechanics of Battlegroups to make things move forward in a timely manner because we only play once a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find Battle Groups easier and more stream-lined than non-battle groups.<br /> <br /> But yeah, to reinforce what other people say, I do think 3rd ed is the best edition. Some of the players found it difficult to grok at first, but they've got the hang of it now. The combats are much more fun, the social system is better (it's not as good as it first appears, and it is a bit more complex, but it's still better), etc. There's a few things people don't love so much, but most of the things we dislike were the same in 2nd ed anyway.<br /> <br /> Certainly no-one's suggested going back to 2nd ed for any of the four games we play.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T02:48:57-07:00","id":1306206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1306095#post1306095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, I guess 3e feels like it's upping the volume Tanith Lee-S&amp;S tone a bit, more than anything else (helped by Minton being pretty good at writing work that hits that feel?). But again, yeah, not mega popular either!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd agree with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:35:34-07:00","id":1306222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1306200#post1306200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am the ST for a game right now. It's great fun even if the mechanics make most fights an entire session just to map out. I heavily, heavily streamline the mechanics of Battlegroups to make things move forward in a timely manner because we only play once a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind if I ask how you go about doing that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T18:15:36-07:00","id":1306376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1306222#post1306222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind if I ask how you go about doing that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just give each Zombie/Thug/Owl-Headed Battle Butler 1 HP and the group's total hp equals the number of members. I don't pin <b>Drill</b> down to anything specific, but what makes sense for the group- Zombies never rout. Thugs rout after losing half their number or a particularly successful 3 point stunt. Soldiers with their Warleader have a bonus on rout checks, etc. It do my best to explain their reactions as what the players see, for example:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>As Forgotten Scholar flashes his blade and three heads tumble down in front of him, Audacious Crow's arrow strikes the brazier holding hours worth of oil and coal. The hundred pound bowl crashes down into the midst of the horde, separating them with a wall of fire as the screams of the pinned-downed bandits are consumed by fire. Captains Bael jumps forward and rips the first bandit he sees clean in half, in a gory display of brutal strength. clearly out matched and surrounded by chaos, the remaining bandits break and all begin running is different directions, caring only for their own lives&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> Forgotten Scholar launched an immediate Decisive attack on his first turn, dealing 3 damage. Crow did a Stunt to bring down a massive flaming bowl of bronze in the middle of the group (crushing 2 guys and triggering a Rout Check), while Bael used grapple charms (on a Battlegroup....) and turned them instantly into damage (while imposing a Morale Penalty for his brutality). The Bandits were promised an easy raid on a peaceful town and barely had any incentives beyond their own desire for loot and panicked, failing their already low morale roll, and broke.<br /> <br /> So in this case 50 bandits were dealt something like 6 wounds, but the Stunts and Scenario caused them to make a Rout check really early and the dice got lucky. When the Bandit Leader, BlackTooth, arrived, he made a command roll to unify them again and pressed the attack, but with less men then he would have.<br /> <br /> It's quick and dirty, and the math is based more on how the scene &quot;feels&quot; then actual stat blocks. I still use the attack stats for when the BG attacks, but I streamline everything else into how you'd expect those foes to react and if they have a leader they get some morale bonuses and stuff.<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh, I forgot, I sometimes change up the 1 Hp - 1 Body thing. The Owl Headed Battle Butlers were all lesser Fae who worked for a Fae queen and had Silver Maces for weapons. They fought in small squads but each one had 3 hp and still worked as a battle group. so 5 bodies, 15 hp, and one goes down at 3, 6, 9... wounds dealt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 04-20-2019, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T20:23:42-07:00","id":1306400,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I\u2019ve been working on streamlining mass combat, so it\u2019s helpful to see how others approach it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T21:36:45-07:00","id":1306428,"title":"","content":"I've been running a 3e game for about 2 years and could see running a 2nd one with all new players at some point. My first game lasted almost 8 years, using 1st and 2nd editions, and I've run another game that lasted 2 years or so. All Solar. I've played in a 2e Lunars game, and the Storyteller will undoubtedly start one for 3e at some point. The 3e core is a mess in many ways, but my players (2 with prior experience and 3 new to Exalted) are really enjoying it. I'm not looking forward to trying to effectively run a combat featuring multiple Exalted antagonists, but at this point regular combats run quite smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T01:42:51-07:00","id":1306475,"title":"","content":"I've been running a Solar campaign ever since the book came out. It's been something like three years.<br /> <br /> And I'm planning a DB one sometime in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T02:26:01-07:00","id":1306479,"title":"","content":"Been playing 2-player games with this since it came out. Currently not in any groups because of time shortage, but I'd like to set something up during the summer.<br /> I find that Exalted, in general, is just a hard system to get into if you aren't already. Makes it hard to get groups started.<br /> That being said, those 2-player games are still incredibly fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T03:03:17-07:00","id":1306489,"title":"","content":"Two-players and one St or one player and one ST? In the latter at the moment but the former is also lots of fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:27:59-07:00","id":1306499,"title":"","content":"We just stopped a Dragon-Blooded game that we could never really get going because we couldn't wrap our heads around Aura in a way that makes sense to us, but now we have started a Solar / Lunar crossover game that shows a lot of promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:32:30-07:00","id":1306501,"title":"","content":"Around a year ago I stopped running my Ex3 game because we pretty much played through all the content in the core book and a serious amount of homebrew. It got to the point where weekly games were quite difficult to prepare because of all the work involved. Before that we played Exalted since 2012 non-stop across all editions.<br /> <br /> Now Dragonblooded are here and I'm looking into getting another game running. I live in a remote area in Germany so finding other Exalted groups to play with is exceedingly difficult. I know only of two other STs. One stopped running Exalted because it's too much work for him and he fell in love with DnD. The other is sadly not running his game online and quite a distance away. So I'm stuck running the game myself if I want to play Ex3.<br /> <br /> But it's very popular with my friends. Maybe even the system that is loved the most. And Ex3 is the most popular edition of the game by far, even though the other ST is playing 1st with his group. But I'm planning on converting him to the glories of Ex3 soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:57:49-07:00","id":1306507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1305787#post1305787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, I think I'm in the only gaming group in town that plays something other than D&amp;D or Pathfinder.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my world. D&amp;D and Pathfinder have a stranglehold on the RPG scene here in Knoxville; getting people interested in anything else is like herding cats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T06:14:17-07:00","id":1306519,"title":"","content":"I have been running a 3rd ed game since the beta corebook was leaked. Now, I run 2 3rd ed games (one online), with characters having essence 5. One of my players started his own 3rd ed game, with another players, while still playing with me.<br /> <br /> Of course, I had to deal with the limited number of books from what we still get by now. What I need and don't have I adapt from earlier editions, improvise, take from the forums or outright create (such as a basic charmset for a Getimian exalted). But even with that, I have less rule problems with 3rd ed than I had with other editions, and the players are having a blast. So, it's been a very positive experience for the edition!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:05:24-07:00","id":1306575,"title":"","content":"I played Ex 1 for half a year or so when it first came out. Later on I was in an Ex2 game for 1 year(?). Through it all and now as well I\u2019ve been part of the \u201cExalted book club\u201d. I would love to play again. However the prep work for running a game seems like such a time commitment. <br /> I\u2019m also working in Tokyo so that limits the number of people I can potentially play with in person compared to a local that has more English speakers. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been thinking of running the quick start as a session or two for some coworkers to just introduce them to the setting and rules, but even that has yet to take place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7142-streetunderbamboo","name":"StreetUnderBamboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T05:46:32-07:00","id":1306809,"title":"","content":"I play 2.5 because my friends all like 2.5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T05:48:30-07:00","id":1306810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1306489#post1306489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two-players and one St or one player and one ST? In the latter at the moment but the former is also lots of fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>One player, one ST. It's... not the traditional tabletop gaming experience, it feels much more like cooperative storytelling.<br /> That's maybe why I like it so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T09:28:43-07:00","id":1306863,"title":"","content":"Been always running one. In terms of playing not as much, as I generally like to stick to Modern/Sci-fi stuff. Fantasy doesn't buzz with me as much anymore (I still like writing stuff for it though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T08:13:53-07:00","id":1307222,"title":"","content":"We are close to ending our second Solar chronicle, and after that it will be a DB Chronicle. But yeah, since the collapse of the local brick and mortar game stores market it has become harder to gauge how many are playing what. I imagine it will be mostly D&amp;D nowadays.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T08:26:24-07:00","id":1307224,"title":"","content":"In general, it seems that the majority of the guys here are actively playing Exalted. I think this is expected, since you guys keep coming to the forum to get ideas, info, etc about a game you are playing. That's cool.<br /> <br /> I think the fanbase has moved from how I remember it. We lost many forumites during The Great Ban Era. It's good to know there are a lot of people playing Ex3.<br /> <br /> I ended an Ex3 campaign about a year ago, but haven't got the time to run another one. We did heavy houseruling to simplify what possible, but I coudn't figure out a good &quot;go-to&quot; method to keep antagonists relevant. <br /> <br /> I'm no expert, but I have this notion that the industry is moving towards simpler more agile systems for tabletop gaming. When I was younger, still studying, and playing Ex1 and Ex2, complex systems didn't bothered me. But I guess I get it now. I really hope that Ex4, if it ever happens, will opt for a different game design philosophy.<br /> <br /> Thank you everyone for sharing your experiences. Keep them coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T09:41:37-07:00","id":1307237,"title":"","content":"That's my impression too, most newer games I see seem a bit simpler. I have to say I feel some are too simple, but while I like Exalted's rules for so many areas other games ignore, it is a bit too complex. Too many variables to keep track of, too many powers to remember.<br /> <br /> Well, that and special dice. That's the other big change I see in game design, and I can't say I love it. I run Star Wars: Edge of the Empire, and I find the special dice don't really match in practice how they work in theory.<br /> <br /> One thing I think Exalted was ahead of the curve in is intimacies. I've started to see other games introduce similar things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-23-2019, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T09:45:10-07:00","id":1307239,"title":"","content":"I will also say that, like Gonzo, I stopped running Solars partly because I found it too much work to challenge the Essence 5 PCs with interesting foes. I've started a new 0xp Lunars game and I am looking forward to actually being able to use stuff from the books without antagonists crumbling like paper tigers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T14:10:44-07:00","id":1307299,"title":"","content":"We're currently in a pause in our Ex3 game to try out a season of a Trinity-Scion hybrid set in the MCU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:41:24-07:00","id":1307529,"title":"","content":"Since it looks like we have the central question here resolved; does anyone know of any active Exalted 3rd Edition Chat games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T12:13:57-07:00","id":1307551,"title":"","content":"I've been ST'ing 3rd edition for a few years. We're 1 session in to our Dragon-Blooded campaign after 40ish sessions of a Solar (+1 Lunar, +1 Alchemical) campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T17:53:21-07:00","id":1307903,"title":"","content":"Sure do! <br /> <br /> We have a World of Darkness / Changing Breeds game on hold, and in the time since Ex3 Core came along we had a fun space game drawing from Fading Suns and other sources, until we thought we had enough Ex3 material to work with.<br /> <br /> We've got a setting and rules hack and having a great time so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:08:32-07:00","id":1307936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1307529#post1307529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it looks like we have the central question here resolved; does anyone know of any active Exalted 3rd Edition Chat games?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in PbP games to read, or to join?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T08:24:13-07:00","id":1308032,"title":"","content":"Since the release I've been playing almost weekly, been through a couple campaigns as a player and another couple as a st.<br /> I have also, more or less once per month, narrated one-shots for newbies on gaming conventions. Several of those were Exalted. I don't keep track of those guys, but a couple told me they're playing campaigns with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T08:53:17-07:00","id":1308037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1307936#post1307936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in PbP games to read, or to join?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, more like a continuous &quot;open world&quot; chat game.<br /> <br /> I like PBP games in theory, but in practice they run out of steam before the 2nd scene finishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T22:01:54-07:00","id":1308887,"title":"","content":"Ah, if it were to read, I would refer you to our ongoing PbP game. Sadly we are not taking on new players at this time, but we\u2019re still going more than a year later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T20:48:29-07:00","id":1309374,"title":"","content":"I have been running EX3 consistently since it dropped. I have run through 2 complete Chronicles so far and played in several games and have run and played in a few immensely enjoyable one shots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T02:24:33-07:00","id":1309394,"title":"","content":"We've stopped playing consistently short time after 2.5e got cancelled. There were attempts to pick it up later, after ex3 release, but they never went far. It was for a multitude of reasons, some of which had nothing to do with Exalted system itself. Some, however, did have something to do with it. For one, obviously, there's not much splats available (and we were not really willing to put time into homebrewing them). Second, we've found that the new attempts were far more narrativist and far less mechanic intensive than before. For some reason even those of us that liked the mechanic side of the game (of which i was one) found 3e to be far less interesting in that regard.<br /> <br /> I mean, storytelling is all and good - i have played a lot of really good campaigns that almost never used any mechanics at all - but one of the things that drew me to Exalted was because i liked tinkering with the mechanics. In ex3, if i had to deal with the mechanic side of something as simple as making a character (or investing xp), i ended finding for myself a ton of excuses to do something else instead. That wasn't a good sign.<br /> <br /> Yes, i know, 2e was broken in so many ways it was really painful, and 3e is a huge improvement in that regard. Too bad however, that, for the most part, i find interacting with 3e charm system to be far more painful (and <i>boring</i>) than in 2e. The system might in theory be far better, but the charms themselves are more boring, and their interaction is way more complicated (and not in a good way). There was something lost on the way.<br /> <br /> That was for Solars. DBs look better, actually. Haven't seen Lunars yet, but i have some hopes here as well. I guess i'll see how the situation evolves in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 05-02-2019, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T14:58:47-07:00","id":1309937,"title":"","content":"Currently running an Ex3 game. After a few years of doubting whether we could handle the crunch, I decided to just do it. It\u2019s going better than expected, and Ex3 is definitely the best Exalted to date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T15:11:46-07:00","id":1310114,"title":"","content":"I basically play free form with 2.5 character sheets for reference. The core book for 3e seemed kind of bloated to me and I didn't want to try to invest myself in refamiliarizing myself with all of it.<br /> <br /> Now I'm hearing exigents are upcoming, and if Lunars are just finishing up then that puts... Abyssals? Sidereals? Next up? The return of the extradimensional Exalted might convince me to dig into 3e more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25282,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","user":"Heart Attacks","date":". 05-05-2019, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","name":"Heart Attacks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25282_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T15:27:19-07:00","id":1310118,"title":"","content":"Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Technically Dragonblood is the only one out, but Lunars is available as raw text. Then Exigents will hopefully be kickstarted in early 2020, and Sidereals in 2021.<br /> <br /> They haven't announced a schedule for the splats beyond that per-se, but I think they'd like to release Getimians after Sidereals (but a small book, not a full hardback like DB or Lunars) and probably Abyssals the year after Sidereals, and Liminals after that (also a smaller book).<br /> <br /> But they've only announced (in terms of fatsplats) Exigents and then Sidereals.<br /> <br /> There's also smaller books scheduled, like the Realm next, a couple of extension books for DBs and Lunars, and Across the Eight Directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2019, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T19:41:06-07:00","id":1310177,"title":"","content":"I would probably be playing more of it if the fanbase (with Holden helping to pile on) hadn't driven my friend who was the biggest Exalted fangirl I knew away from the game when she dared criticize some content that hit close to her identity, but after a long stretch of not playing it at all I'm finally in a DB game, running a Lunar game, and in a mixed-celestial (Solars and my Lunar) game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T21:05:13-07:00","id":1310197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310177#post1310177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably be playing more of it if the fanbase (with Holden helping to pile on) hadn't driven my friend who was the biggest Exalted fangirl I knew away from the game when she dared criticize some content that hit close to her identity, but after a long stretch of not playing it at all I'm finally in a DB game, running a Lunar game, and in a mixed-celestial (Solars and my Lunar) game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you can get her back into Exalted. I wasn\u2019t around then, but I have found the community to be largely supportive and helpful since I started playing a bit over a year ago. The Devs and moderators here are really open and helpful, and certainly don\u2019t tolerate harassment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T23:05:56-07:00","id":1310219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310197#post1310197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope you can get her back into Exalted. I wasn\u2019t around then, but I have found the community to be largely supportive and helpful since I started playing a bit over a year ago. The Devs and moderators here are really open and helpful, and certainly don\u2019t tolerate harassment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the new pair of devs are a vast improvement, but that bridge is burned, those fields are salted, and that city is a radioactive crater. She can't even stand to look at Exalted stuff now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 05-06-2019, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T03:24:33-07:00","id":1310251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310219#post1310219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the new pair of devs are a vast improvement, but that bridge is burned, those fields are salted, and that city is a radioactive crater. She can't even stand to look at Exalted stuff now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two really did a lot to tarnish the game for me, too, and though I didn't call them out myself, a lot of my distaste for the game is focused around their progressively tone deaf handling of the game and the game's community interaction and particularly some really unpleasant personal encounters with one of them. I had backed the Exalted 3e Deluxe from launch day and had cancelled mostly due to not wanting to support the line on principal before it finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","name":"Heart Attacks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25282_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T03:58:36-07:00","id":1310255,"title":"","content":"Previous devs were almost complete opposites in online style. Morke made distant pronouncements and generally didn't seem to like interacting online at all very much (thought it was a waste of time and source of bad ideas I'd guess). Holden was a fierce, brash, hyperbolic poster who would go extremely far in rhetoric and sometimes to his opponent's character in order to win every argument and sell every aspect of his personal vision without compromise, rather than subject his ideas to any sort of examination. <br /> <br /> Some of their ideas were bad (mostly towards their 2e run) and good (mostly when they went back to 1e with fresh eyes to refocus and repurpose Exalted back to its original genre and aims, as they understood it).<br /> <br /> I do think if more people had spoken out about the excesses of Holden's online style at the time, rather than enthusiastically liking every post in which he 'dunked' on an opponent while driving argument to ever higher rhetorical extremes, then we might have checked this sort of behavior a bit more, so some of the after-the-fact condemnation rings a bit hollow. Especially when my impression is some of these people commenting now may be the people who imitated that rhetorical style to the greatest extent, and liked it when they weren't its subject... But anyway there's not much point talking over this and it's all verging into personal attack territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T07:04:44-07:00","id":1310278,"title":"","content":"I don't play Exalted 3e. Then again, I didn't play 2e either, nor any of the other RPGs I'm interested in. It's more about my own situation than the game. I've always been more of a reader than a player, but I will change that some day. I still read the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T08:39:24-07:00","id":1310293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310177#post1310177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably be playing more of it if the fanbase (with Holden helping to pile on) hadn't driven my friend who was the biggest Exalted fangirl I knew away from the game when she dared criticize some content that hit close to her identity, but after a long stretch of not playing it at all I'm finally in a DB game, running a Lunar game, and in a mixed-celestial (Solars and my Lunar) game.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm curious what that was. I'd like to prevent something like that from happening in the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310255#post1310255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I do think if more people had spoken out about the excesses of Holden's online style at the time, rather than enthusiastically liking every post in which he 'dunked' on an opponent while driving argument to ever higher rhetorical extremes, then we might have checked this sort of behavior a bit more, so some of the after-the-fact condemnation rings a bit hollow. Especially when my impression is some of these people commenting now may be the people who imitated that rhetorical style to the greatest extent, and liked it when they weren't its subject... But anyway there's not much point talking over this and it's all verging into personal attack territory.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's important to consider Holden's background. He didn't come from nowhere and bring toxicity with him, he was a veteran member of this community who became a writer and eventually developer. A major part of why people didn't call out him dunking on people is because those moments of unprofessionalism are an aspect of this community that goes back much further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T09:31:50-07:00","id":1310301,"title":"","content":"Lioness, you're right of course, and that is an appropriate correction on my statement above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:59:01-07:00","id":1310335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310293#post1310293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm curious what that was. I'd like to prevent something like that from happening in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't on this forum. The very short version is that we said that the way Rose-Lipped Seduction Style was fluffed and interacted with the social rules felt like asexual erasure to her, and a few other posters spoke up about feeling the same, and the reaction was surprisingly vicious for the site where this happened. I would indeed hope the reaction would be better here in the present.<br /> <br /> And within the game itself, the way the DB and Lunar sex-related Charms are very specifically written is a vast improvement from trying to use the Red and Orichalcum rules to deflect any and all criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T13:28:03-07:00","id":1310360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially when my impression is some of these people commenting now may be the people who imitated that rhetorical style to the greatest extent, and liked it when they weren't its subject... </div> </div> </div>The idea that it was the duty of the people who were being driven away by the poor behavior of the devs to instead reign them in and reform the community is kind of ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25282,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","user":"Heart Attacks","date":". 05-06-2019, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","name":"Heart Attacks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25282_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T18:38:40-07:00","id":1310441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heart Attacks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310360#post1310360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea that it was the duty of the people who were being driven away by the poor behavior of the devs to instead reign them in and reform the community is kind of ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less ridiculous than you think, because you are presuming that'd be a primary or definitive solution, and it doesn't have to be to exist.<br /> <br /> You can't escape from that problem. Social categorizations are inevitable, and that fluke is a natural side effect.<br /> <br /> One of the workarounds for that problem is exactly having the affected parties make themselves heard. It's literally the only way to raise the issue when other parties are already participating in the aggravating behavior.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T19:12:04-07:00","id":1310449,"title":"","content":"People weren't silent about their feelings, so? The community was full of people who rallied around Holden and Morke and doubled down on defending their behavior (&amp; their ideas, I guess.) There was some serious idol worship around the dev team during the transition era between the end of 2.5 and 3e.<br /> <br /> But so like no, nobody is obligated to participate in (let alone to take responsibility for) a community that alienates them, especially when it's for something as disposable as RPG discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25282,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","user":"Heart Attacks","date":". 05-06-2019, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","name":"Heart Attacks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25282_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T19:54:48-07:00","id":1310457,"title":"","content":"You are absolutely correct, no one is obligated to participate. And exercising that right already constitutes a way to tell the main group they are fucking up. It's effectiveness is debatable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T03:33:08-07:00","id":1310507,"title":"","content":"Most of the pushback against their behavior was on other fora and Heart Attacks is quite right in asserting that the hero worship here did not leave room for critical feedback. Those two are gone, however, so it's a bit of a moot point. The only thing that matters now is undoing the damage to the brand and convincing the larger community that Ex3 is under new management and back on track.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T07:43:40-07:00","id":1310532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heart Attacks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310449#post1310449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was some serious idol worship around the dev team during the transition era between the end of 2.5 and 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me, it goes back further than that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T09:22:46-07:00","id":1310552,"title":"","content":"When Holden was just a normal poster, and when he was an Ink Monkey, he always seemed pretty reasonable to me. The aggressive views towards anyone who criticised him I think only came much later. (His twitter has become much more angry and aggressive over time as well.) So I can see Lioness's point about a toxic environment.<br /> <br /> Same with John Morke actually, I remember debating with him about some stuff when he was an Ink Monkey, and actually criticising his work (I said his charms were way too long) and he was okay. You know, we respecetfully disagreed, but he listened and said he'd take on board people's opinions. Whereas I know later people made quite serious complaints about him.<br /> <br /> Some of the stuff they got really angry about being criticised for (like the Abyssal Presence preview), I think is the sort of thing they'd have taken in much better back when they were Ink Monkeys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T09:33:04-07:00","id":1310553,"title":"","content":"So, anyway, moving on.<br /> <br /> As I said, I play two Celestial games (one is just reaching Essence 5, the other is on like 450xp not counting Solar xp), which are continuations of 2nd ed games, and so have been going about... 11-12 years?<br /> But I also started running an all-Lunar game recently. I wanted to try out the game at 0xp, which I haven't done for ages. So far it's been good, but it's only 2 sessions.<br /> <br /> My friends also play a Solar game which has reached Essence 3, and a Dragonblood game which continued from 2nd ed, it's been going about 2-3 years I think, so also Essence 3 maybe?<br /> <br /> Out of interest, anyone else who plays more than one game (or has started a new one), how similar/different do you find the games?<br /> <br /> Both of the Celestial games I play are in the South, both are high-xp (as they've been going so long), though both mostly have characters who'd feel appropriate in a lower game (though the essence 5 game has 2 characters who would absolutely not feel appropriate in a 0xp game). Both are mostly around one area controlled by the PCs, but used to be more globe-trotting.<br /> <br /> Neither game has fought the Realm or Raksha much so far. One game featured a lot of undead in the past but not now, the other game features a lot of undead now but not in the past. Both games have a Lunar girl with enormous Appearance. Both games used to feature a Malfeas/Cecylene Infernal.<br /> <br /> So while they are different, they're not radically different (we used to say one game was much more grimdark than the other, but that's no longer the case).<br /> <br /> I wonder if others have found that, or your two+ games are very different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T10:38:26-07:00","id":1310571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310177#post1310177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably be playing more of it if the fanbase (with Holden helping to pile on) hadn't driven my friend who was the biggest Exalted fangirl I knew away from the game when she dared criticize some content that hit close to her identity, but after a long stretch of not playing it at all I'm finally in a DB game, running a Lunar game, and in a mixed-celestial (Solars and my Lunar) game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please tell her that she's more important to the game and its spirit, than the game is to most of us (sorry if that doesn't make sense, I swear I mean something positive). I'm sorry she had such a bad experience. We exalted fans should be on the same side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T10:58:16-07:00","id":1310579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310507#post1310507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those two are gone, however, so it's a bit of a moot point. The only thing that matters now is undoing the damage to the brand and convincing the larger community that Ex3 is under new management and back on track.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep thinking that the wall raised against criticism to their vision affected the final Ex3 book. I agree with others that have stated that the core looks like a good first manuscript, but that much editing was needed.<br /> <br /> The new devs write shorter charms, and have made (as far as I can tell) charmtrees which are easier to navigate. However, some overdesigned things from the core have carried over to the new material. For me, Ex3 was the chance to finally have a clean system. But each day that passes I'm more convinced that a serious revision of some rules is very needed.<br /> <br /> I may be a minority here, I see a lot of guys playing just fine. But I want to play Exalted again and feel it is a game I can handle, in which my old friends can come back again without feeling like we're gonna play &quot;homework: the game&quot;. I keep crossing my fingers for a potential solution for my needs. I know it sounds selfish, but hey! I've been playing since 2001, I think I deserve some kind of spiritual cookie haha.<br /> <br /> Maybe the ST guide can be a good start. Remember when power combat appeared (that was in the player's guide), and let us play the same game in a new way (not saying a necessarily better way)? I'd be 100% interested in something that could simplify Ex3 and still kept all the valuable stuff in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 05-07-2019, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T12:27:36-07:00","id":1310596,"title":"","content":"So with 2e, they acknowledged the problems with their system late in the game line, attempted to account for it in their current work pretty hard (I don't remember who said it or where, that Infernals mechanics were a love letter to the game Exalted wanted to be), and eventually patched the entire system in one massive shot after everything was done.<br /> <br /> I really hope that if the current team finds themselves feeling similarly about 3e (that it has problems that are intractable and need to be fixed for a healthy game), that they do that patch somewhere in the middle rather than way at the end.<br /> <br /> I totally agree that I'd love an Exalted that I didn't need to study extensively before I could run it with a reasonable understanding of the rules. I feel like whenever I try to get back to Exalted I end up with a rules-light thing that roughly acknowledges everyone's character sheet and that's not really what I want (still at 2.5 though, still haven't waded into the 3e books much yet.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25282-heart-attacks","name":"Heart Attacks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25282_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:39:25-07:00","id":1310650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310579#post1310579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be a minority here, I see a lot of guys playing just fine. But I want to play Exalted again and feel it is a game I can handle, in which my old friends can come back again without feeling like we're gonna play &quot;homework: the game&quot;. I keep crossing my fingers for a potential solution for my needs. I know it sounds selfish, but hey! I've been playing since 2001, I think I deserve some kind of spiritual cookie haha.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my experience that it is easier to play than it appears. I barely had to filter more than chargen to get quick adventures running for absolute newbies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T11:34:11-07:00","id":1310779,"title":"","content":"I played in a mixed mortal to Solar/Lunar game, a mixed Celestial game and ran an Infernals game all in 2/2.5.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to play a Ex3 game but my schedule is relatively restrictive (and I'm in 3 other games currently) but my schedule was highly incompatible with my previous group (specifically that Weekend daytime games just don't work for me when they were the best times for everyone else) who have gone on to play several Ex3 games. <br /> <br /> Someday hopefully, I'll find a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T11:36:42-07:00","id":1312608,"title":"","content":"Weekly with our gaming group... is pretty awesome in my opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 05-17-2019, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T12:51:38-07:00","id":1312628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310650#post1310650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's my experience that it is easier to play than it appears. I barely had to filter more than chargen to get quick adventures running for absolute newbies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. A lot of the systems look a pretty daunting on paper. But really, after a bit of practice, I've found that it clicks a lot of the time with players.<br /> <br /> That's why I recommend running the game RAW with few, if any, house rules before you dive in. I mean... Things like if you're gonna change XP to flat costs rather than exponential, yeah you can probably do that from the start, but give the combat systems a try before you throw it out. Maybe poke at Craft before deciding what you want to prune. (Except Project Slots, I haven't ever seen something to justify them. How many projects do most Crafters have going on at a time?)<br /> <br /> Just... The game LOOKS more complex and intimidating when you're just reading it than it actually plays out, in my experience.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">And that, kids, is why White Room Theorycrafting is Near-Useless for discussing mechanics.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-16-2019, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T15:29:17-07:00","id":1312659,"title":"","content":"I'm in 3 Solar games at the moment, with all 3 groups running sessions roughly once every 2 weeks.<br /> <br /> The 1st game has been going on for about 2 years and our Circle has just reached Essence 3 after splatting Alhat.<br /> <br /> The other 2 games are a few months old and I'm the ST in them. They're my first experience as ST and I'm having a blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T16:30:26-07:00","id":1312667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3#post1305783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, how many people are actually playing this latest edition?<br /> <br /> I'm currently just reading the books, and sometimes I come here to the forums to see if there's been any exciting news.<br /> <br /> How about you, or the players near you? Would you say Ex3 is popular as a gaming option? Or is it more like a setting that people like to read but can't actually get the time, the friends, or whatever to play it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\\<br /> <br /> The following is all my opinion:<br /> <br /> I'm currently STing a game in a PBP fashion for a group of six on GITP, and I had to drop a couple of other applicants (sadly). So there are definitely players out there.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue in my experience is that it is very hard to find anyone willing to ST the game. (I don't say this as a boast, I speak from personal experience; I HAAATE GMing and am really bad at it but after a year and a half to two years of games never making it past character creation I decided to just bite the bullet and try it) It's got a fun, unique setting that is absolutely worth playing a game or two.<br /> <br /> A second issue that is also pretty massive is that it's a hard game to get into. The corebook is difficult to navigate and very poorly formatted, with information important to the game scattered and hard to find. One example that came up during my game is the issue of decisive damage: Decisive damage does not deal double 10s. You'd think this would be under Decisive damage, but no; it's under *withering* damage. And it's shown in reverse. &quot;Unlike decisive attacks, the Double 10s rule does apply to withering damage rolls.&quot; Also I'm not really sure where it says that double 10s are a thing to begin with; I'm sure it does I'm just not sure where. Now, this is obviously something that will be remedied with time, as we get used to the system and learn its various ins and outs. But if I don't devote time to the game because the corebook is initially confusing, I'll never hit that point. And it's difficult to do a good long game of Exalted without delving into multiple Exalt types; which the corebook does not have.<br /> <br /> However, Exalted's setting is very entertaining, imaginative (or more to the point, imagination stirring) and unique, and it's a refreshing departure from D&amp;D and its various iterations (which, like it or not, are currently the most popular TTRPGs). And once you actually get the game running and know what you're doing, it's very fun and engaging. Just enough is established for the world to feel real, but enough is left mysterious and undefined that your own personal Creation can have a very unique feel compared to anyone else's. This is pretty ubiquitous across good TTRPGs, but Exalted has a more cinematic anime/wuxia feel to it that you don't really get anywhere else. Your characters are also exceedingly strong from the get-go and can get even stronger over time, but you can never let your guard down entirely. And hey, if you're bored with one character type (Solars) you can move to another (Lunar, DB, etc) and enjoy what they have to offer. Each provides characters that &quot;feel&quot; different, even if you do the same basic concept; a Solar Swordswoman is going to feel very different from a Lunar Swordsman.<br /> <br /> So in short: the game is hard to get into, but once you do, there's a ton of fun to be had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T18:57:35-07:00","id":1312688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1312628#post1312628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. A lot of the systems look a pretty daunting on paper. But really, after a bit of practice, I've found that it clicks a lot of the time with players.<br /> <br /> That's why I recommend running the game RAW with few, if any, house rules before you dive in. I mean... Things like if you're gonna change XP to flat costs rather than exponential, yeah you can probably do that from the start, but give the combat systems a try before you throw it out. Maybe poke at Craft before deciding what you want to prune. (Except Project Slots, I haven't ever seen something to justify them. How many projects do most Crafters have going on at a time?)<br /> <br /> Just... The game LOOKS more complex and intimidating when you're just reading it than it actually plays out, in my experience.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">And that, kids, is why White Room Theorycrafting is Near-Useless for discussing mechanics.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>We did three or four playtest sessions with the raw core. Two or three players plus me.<br /> <br /> We had a bit of a hitch coming from a tactical + squares + ranges + initiative is just time perspective into the cinematic + range as camera + initiative is also being on a roll perspective. But I adored it right out of the gate and my players started getting into it.<br /> <br /> The reason I did the Momentum rewrite though is that we kept coming out of the game in order to do iterations of arithmetic , sort , choose ; and then to remember which actions had a +1 cost or a double 10 or not or whatever. We got the number of items to remember back down under average human memory limitations, and found ourselves very rarely leaving the game to do math and lookup anymore. <br /> <br /> I'm not at all saying this to complain. Rather, to say that I found the raw core rules to be a very high pinnacle of new ideas, from which I could see a brand new place I wanted my games to go. <br /> <br /> We're having a great time, which reminds me that I was going to go post a story over in my other thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T23:05:36-07:00","id":1312720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1312628#post1312628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. A lot of the systems look a pretty daunting on paper. But really, after a bit of practice, I've found that it clicks a lot of the time with players.<br /> <br /> That's why I recommend running the game RAW with few, if any, house rules before you dive in. I mean... Things like if you're gonna change XP to flat costs rather than exponential, yeah you can probably do that from the start, but give the combat systems a try before you throw it out. Maybe poke at Craft before deciding what you want to prune. (Except Project Slots, I haven't ever seen something to justify them. How many projects do most Crafters have going on at a time?)<br /> <br /> Just... The game LOOKS more complex and intimidating when you're just reading it than it actually plays out, in my experience.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">And that, kids, is why White Room Theorycrafting is Near-Useless for discussing mechanics.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna second (third?) this. All the systems jive with each other far better than prior editions. Even with having to walk new players through things like combat things take less time overall. Everything speeds up even further with people who've become more comfortable with it. Scary text, intuitive in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T07:38:34-07:00","id":1312753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1312667#post1312667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm currently STing a game in a PBP fashion for a group of six on GITP</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey neat! My group is also on GitP! Mind dropping a link? I\u2019d like to see what ya\u2019ll are doing differently from us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T08:23:59-07:00","id":1312758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sticks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1312753#post1312753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey neat! My group is also on GitP! Mind dropping a link? I\u2019d like to see what ya\u2019ll are doing differently from us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The IC thread here: <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?584767-Exalted-3e-Of-Tri-Khans-and-God-Kings-IC\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...d-God-Kings-IC</a><br /> <br /> The OOC thread here: <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?583961-Exalted-3e-Of-Tri-Khans-and-God-Kings-OOC\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...-God-Kings-OOC</a><br /> <br /> We're also using a Discord server to coordinate a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T13:13:26-07:00","id":1313005,"title":"","content":"I've been running a 2.5E game for almost a year - and I'm hesitant about shifting to 3E until I see how Alchemicals are handled in it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T11:27:00-07:00","id":1313528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1310650#post1310650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's my experience that it is easier to play than it appears. I barely had to filter more than chargen to get quick adventures running for absolute newbies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's been my experience too. Amusingly one of my newbies pointed to motes as one of the most overly complicated parts of the system, she plays a crafter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T16:48:32-07:00","id":1313937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1312628#post1312628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. A lot of the systems look a pretty daunting on paper. But really, after a bit of practice, I've found that it clicks a lot of the time with players.<br /> <br /> That's why I recommend running the game RAW with few, if any, house rules before you dive in. I mean... Things like if you're gonna change XP to flat costs rather than exponential, yeah you can probably do that from the start, but give the combat systems a try before you throw it out. Maybe poke at Craft before deciding what you want to prune. (Except Project Slots, I haven't ever seen something to justify them. How many projects do most Crafters have going on at a time?)<br /> <br /> Just... The game LOOKS more complex and intimidating when you're just reading it than it actually plays out, in my experience.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">And that, kids, is why White Room Theorycrafting is Near-Useless for discussing mechanics.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. My opinion is that the game system is quite well designed, apart from the awfully clunky Craft system of course. I don't think many people love that one (not because it is difficult, it is very easy to understand, just super clunky and downright stupid). Personally I have some issues with how creating your own evocations is explained as well, but maybe that is just me. Anyway, maybe the evocation part isn't fantastic (I find myself just using existing artifacts, but maybe it is just me being bad at mechanics), but again, that could be me.<br /> But yes, it is a fantastic game with an even more fantastic setting !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T18:12:46-07:00","id":1313957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1313937#post1313937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. My opinion is that the game system is quite well designed, apart from the awfully clunky Craft system of course. I don't think many people love that one (not because it is difficult, it is very easy to understand, just super clunky and downright stupid). Personally I have some issues with how creating your own evocations is explained as well, but maybe that is just me. Anyway, maybe the evocation part isn't fantastic (I find myself just using existing artifacts, but maybe it is just me being bad at mechanics), but again, that could be me.<br /> But yes, it is a fantastic game with an even more fantastic setting !</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah no, the book is NOT very homebrew-friendly. That's why I'm waiting for the Exigent book.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, you can make your own Charms for Splats, or for Evocations, or your own Martial Art Styles! Go nuts!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Great! Any advice on how to do that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Psh, <i>no</i>. What you expect a core book to tell you how to do the things it recommends?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T19:08:45-07:00","id":1313966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305783-do-you-play-ex3?p=1313957#post1313957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah no, the book is NOT very homebrew-friendly. That's why I'm waiting for the Exigent book.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, you can make your own Charms for Splats, or for Evocations, or your own Martial Art Styles! Go nuts!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Great! Any advice on how to do that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Psh, <i>no</i>. What you expect a core book to tell you how to do the things it recommends?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, yes, that is exactly how I feel concerning evocations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T06:52:05-07:00","id":1314055,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I found all of that pretty useless and frustrating. Especially where being able to add Evocations was the signature of a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}